Package: sabinaJMBM
Title: Joint Multiscale Bayesian species distribution modelling using INLA
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("First", "Last", , "first.last@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "YOUR-ORCID-ID"))
Description: Bayesian implementation of nested species distribution models 
    (NSDMs) integrating global and regional data through hierarchical
    coupling in INLA via 'inlabru'. Accepts NSDM objects and implements
    joint spatial Bayesian models with stochastic partial differential
    equation (SPDE) random effects. Provides multiple coupling architectures
    (unpooled, ordered hierarchical, scale-decomposed, Bayesian feedback)
    for distinguishing scale-dependent niche dimensions and addressing niche
    truncation. Improves predictive stability in non-analogous future climates
    when regional training data lack geographic breadth of species' true ranges.
